                        ],
                        "form": "misrun"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fa9f7bb9-5f99-3454-8074-7c5f88667a72",
                        "entry_id": "8d7c70de-9769-3100-b636-34c9fdb17828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To run incompetently; mismanage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "53207483-e66a-44c8-8fc8-45d32b3e7a75",
                                "sense_id": "fa9f7bb9-5f99-3454-8074-7c5f88667a72",
                                "text": "The men who are misrunning the Peace show are the same political muddlers who misran the war show."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "12ad77ba-dfb0-48b5-8c1d-0327696ac93b",
                                "sense_id": "fa9f7bb9-5f99-3454-8074-7c5f88667a72",
                                "text": "Certainly the main aim of many liberals and reformers in the Soviet Union's provinces in the Gorbachev era was to outwit the central institutions of power: the Kremlin, the armed forces, the bureaucrats who ran (or misran) the planned economy, and most of all the cold grey men of the KGB."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "16698d80-e81a-4d17-a73a-45e372b5c4df",
                                "sense_id": "fa9f7bb9-5f99-3454-8074-7c5f88667a72",
                                "text": "Perhaps I had simply had enough...of NTFC being misrun by yet another businessman who did not seem to care, of constant worries about whether the club had a future."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "146dd28b-0555-314f-b904-a829cff1c5ec",
                        "entry_id": "8d7c70de-9769-3100-b636-34c9fdb17828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To result in a misrun."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "04aa9bd2-1d39-4b72-8b92-017e7c270625",
                                "sense_id": "146dd28b-0555-314f-b904-a829cff1c5ec",
                                "text": "One set of bars misran, while others showed a coarsely crystalline structure, which is more often due to too hot pouring than to any other ."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee414292-f86f-4e98-b8cd-cbffd7e99168",
                                "sense_id": "146dd28b-0555-314f-b904-a829cff1c5ec",
                                "text": "Those having light work on their floors would have several pieces misrun, but the losses from this cause in many instances would not, in the aggregate, amount to 4 per cent of the total value of the work poured in any one heat, consequently they would not be paid for the work so lost."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8972a9d6-8561-4d3f-9f97-20d150d130b4",
                                "sense_id": "146dd28b-0555-314f-b904-a829cff1c5ec",
                                "text": "According to the speaker, early castings made of the thorium containing alloys misran on sections that normally should fill easily."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "020863af-edd7-3ae9-aa03-9738e52d8440",
                        "entry_id": "8d7c70de-9769-3100-b636-34c9fdb17828",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To run badly or off-course."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "725fa10b-3a16-438c-8b0c-d90d53b208bc",
                                "sense_id": "020863af-edd7-3ae9-aa03-9738e52d8440",
                                "text": "In the frustrate strife Of the vanquisht life, On the course misrun To the goal unwon By the faith, self-cheated Of the deed defeated, To claim our home."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "233b73f5-db6d-46ec-a6e9-c75b5c93a94f",
                                "sense_id": "020863af-edd7-3ae9-aa03-9738e52d8440",
                                "text": "The torpedo left correctly, but the track was not observed from the Princess Royal, and it possibly misran badly and was the torpedo seen to cross the Inflexible's bows at 2035."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9c76b90c-1ca8-40d9-83d8-aea6cb60a3c7",
                                "sense_id": "020863af-edd7-3ae9-aa03-9738e52d8440",
                                "text": "Two of them misran while five hit, sinking three ships and damaging one beyond repair, totalling 14,500 tons – a very respectable performance."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "24b998a7-3ae4-4ee4-a3d0-9a8c926267fe",
                                "sense_id": "020863af-edd7-3ae9-aa03-9738e52d8440",
                                "text": "Slap that MERKLES HAPPEN bumper sticker on your shiny new Model T and praise the Lord some dumb nineteen-year-old rookie misran the bases."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
